{"id": "EUVD-2026-97048", "enisaUuid": "6069adbf-9ef9-333b-9d48-2a10256556ea", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to assign or remove department heads by calling PUT /sys/user/changeDepartChargePerson. Low-privileged attackers can supply arbitrary userId, department id, and status values to make any user a department head, widening department-scoped views, or demote existing heads.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:33:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:13:30", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_user_depart_charge_person.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysUserController.java#L2007-L2011", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-user-changedepartchargeperson"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108874", "GHSA-v9j5-w9hf-2fc2"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "97bb52d9-63a3-35a1-8c61-41718e23823a", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "216ce8dc-b0d2-381f-8946-26f315adae81", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}